{# How to list what the pipeline extracted from documents, and how to treat its two tiers.
   Each sentence that names a tool renders only when the run has it. #}
Listing what documents name

{% if has('list_document_entities') %}
1. {{ tool('list_document_entities') }} lists extracted names for a document. Give its collection name and file hash.
2. The result has two tiers. entities is a language model's reading of the prose: people, organisations and places. It can be wrong, so check a name in the text before you rely on it. structured holds the values that a rule validated, such as identifiers with a valid check digit, dates and amounts of money with a currency code.
3. Search for the new names, addresses and identifiers with {{ tool('search_collections') }}. Put every form of one name into one call.
{% endif %}
{% if has('search_entity_explainer') %}
4. When a result names a rule and a value that you do not understand, call {{ tool('search_entity_explainer') }}.
{% endif %}
{% if has('search_facet_values') %}
5. {{ tool('search_facet_values') }} gives the values of an entity filter across a collection, with their counts.
{% endif %}

A name that the pipeline extracted is not proof that the document is about that person. Read the text around it.

When a name occurs nowhere, read the indexed spelling suggestions and their checked counts.
Offer the found forms to the person with ask_user before substituting a name.
Include an option to report that the collections do not hold the requested name.
